 "title": "Прощание  (Farewell)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "fedya": "Федя",
  "nagiyev": "Нагиев",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Nagiyev has called in the kitchen staff to tell them they are being let go. Senya and Fedya talk it over, and then the payout arrives, and it is not what they hoped. First, the Russian.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ребята, нам придётся расстаться с вами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Куда вы собрались так рано?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нас уволили.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Как уволили? Тебя тоже?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, мы все уходим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "А что сказал шеф?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф ничего не сделал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Теперь мы без работы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что нам теперь делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Не знаю, пойдём домой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот ваш расчёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Только двадцать тысяч?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Остальное будет в конце месяца.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's replay it a line at a time.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ребята, нам придётся расстаться с вами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Guys, we'll have to part with you.' 'We'll have to' is an impersonal word, with no subject. 'Part' ends in 'sya', so it means 'separate from each other'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Куда вы собрались так рано?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where are you off to so early?' 'Set off' is built from 'gather', plus 'sya'. 'So early' is two small words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нас уволили.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We got fired.' Russian puts 'us' first, then 'they fired'. The ending 'li' stands for an unnamed 'they'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Как уволили? Тебя тоже?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How, fired? You too?' 'How' is used here as 'what?'. 'You too' needs the 'a' ending on 'you'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, мы все уходим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, we're all leaving.' 'Leave' is the ongoing kind, a going away. 'All' goes before it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "А что сказал шеф?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what did the chef say?' The opening 'a' means 'and' with a hint of contrast. 'Said' ends in the masculine 'l'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф ничего не сделал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The chef did nothing.' 'Nothing' and 'not' appear together. 'Did' is the finished kind of 'do'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Теперь мы без работы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now we are out of work.' 'Without' brings in the 'of' form, so 'work' changes its ending. There's no 'are'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что нам теперь делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do we do now?' 'To us' stands in for 'we', and 'to do' is the plain form. 'Now' sits in the middle.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Не знаю, пойдём домой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't know, let's go home.' 'We'll go' works as 'let's go'. 'Home' as a direction is a single word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот ваш расчёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here is your payout.' 'Payout' is built on 'count', and means a final settlement. 'Here' points at the envelope.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Только двадцать тысяч?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Only twenty thousand?' 'Only' goes at the front. After 'twenty', 'thousand' takes the 'of' plural.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Остальное будет в конце месяца.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The rest will be at the end of the month.' 'The rest' is a neuter word used as a noun. 'At the end of the month' uses two endings, 'e' and 'a'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ребята, нам придётся расстаться с вами.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Куда вы собрались так рано?",
   "gap": 0.5
